<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wartislaw I, Duke of Pomerania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1120s–1130s</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Wartislaw I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wartislaw I (fl. 1120s–1130s) was the first historically attested Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerania">Pomerania</a> and ancestor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-griffins">Griffin dynasty</a>. He united Slavic tribes around the lower Oder and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/szczecin">Szczecin</a>, accepted the overlordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-iii-wrymouth">Bolesław III Wrymouth</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-of-bamberg">Otto of Bamberg</a>'s mission to convert his people. He was later killed by a pagan, and a monastery at Stolpe on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peene">Peene</a> was founded in his memory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wartislaw-i-duke-of-pomerania.jpg" alt="Wartislaw I, Duke of Pomerania" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Erell · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stolpe_Wartislawkirche_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
